CommitDate: Sun Oct 25 17:28:59 2026 -0500

    fix(board): enforce repo-local board lint. Addresses DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55.
    
    The board-lint pre-commit hook was inert twice over: a global
    core.hooksPath (/var/tmp/foreign-hooks) made git ignore .git/hooks, and
    the repo-local hook's managed block ran boardctl validate in warn mode
    whose reject branch never returned non-zero.
    
    - scripts/hooks/pre-commit (new, tracked): gitreins guard subshell +
      fail-closed board-lint; validation failures reject the commit and the
      validator output names the offending id; tooling problems (missing
      board/boardctl/timeout, rc 124) still skip and never wedge commits.
    - scripts/install-hooks.sh (new, tracked): installs the tracked hook
      into the repo's own hooks dir (--git-common-dir, worktree-safe) and,
      when a non-local core.hooksPath shadows it, sets a repo-local
      core.hooksPath override. Only .git/config is written; global/user
      config and the foreign hooks dir are untouched. Idempotent, backs up
      a differing pre-existing hook.
    - scripts/tests/install-hooks-selftest.sh + make install-hooks{,-selftest}
      + CONTRIBUTING.md "Git hooks" section.
    
    Verified: in this checkout git now resolves pre-commit to
    .git/hooks/pre-commit and grep 'boardctl_lint_mode="warn"' exits 1; in a
    throwaway clone a duplicate-id commit was rejected (rc=1, HEAD unmoved,
    output names "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-55") and a valid board row still commits.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
